                // ---- The garrison headquarters — the main building, and you walk INTO it
                // The user, 2026-08-12: „auch das main gebäude in dem der gas und schwert
                // nachschub ist muss da sein (in das gebäude muss man rein laufen können.
                // drinnen sind die nachschübe)". Until today the hub was three pads on open
                // ground; this is the place they belong in.
                //
                // ## Where, and why here and not "wherever there is room"
                //
                // A garrison headquarters holds the gate and it holds the supply. This one
                // stands **on the west side of the main street, one block inside the inner
                // gate**, its front door on the two-gate axis and the market square with the
                // church directly opposite: the civic centre of the district, at the point
                // every sortie passes through anyway. Its back is the canal quay (x = -55),
                // which is how a depot took delivery before it took lorries.
                // The player's spawn point (0, 2, 0) stands **15 m in front of the door and
                // looking at it**.
                //
                // ⚠️ The site is bounded on all four sides and the numbers are not free:
                //   x >= -47   the canal quay ends at x = -55, and the bridges reach x = -52
                //   x <= -15   the main street apron runs x = -15..15; the facade is flush
                //              with it, so the door opens straight onto the pavement
                //   |z| <= 13  the gantry columns of the swing spine stand at z = +-13.5..21.5
                //              (x = -18..-10). Half a metre of clearance, and it is the reason
                //              the hall is 26 m deep and not 40.
                //
                // ## THERE IS NO SUBTRACTION — the doorway is a GAP, not a hole
                //
                // `FIND-056` records what this costs when it is forgotten: the wall's decorative
                // plinth was emitted across the full run while the courses above it carried the
                // openings, and the gate measured `height 2.000` — solid. So the east facade is
                // **three blocks and not one**: a south segment, a north segment and a lintel
                // that starts at y = 4.5. Nothing else in this building crosses z = -3..3 at
                // x = -16.5..-15. The one thing that does run through the opening is the base
                // slab, and it is 0.15 m of floor, deliberately (see below).
                //
                // ## The base slab does three jobs and that is why it is one block
                //
                // 1. It is the **floor** — a depot floor a foot above the street, which is what
                //    keeps stores dry and what a threshold is.
                // 2. It is the **apron**: a generated house is dropped as soon as a placed block
                //    overlaps it, and 8 m of row house against a roof at 11.0 m does NOT overlap.
                //    Without the slab the layout builds houses inside the hall.
                // 3. It is the **measurement**: 0.15 m is the only floor height in this map
                //    (ground 0.0, aprons 0.05, quays and bridges 0.4), so `assert height > 0.10`
                //    in `scripts/f019-hq.txt` is a position bracket that only the interior
                //    satisfies. The step at the door is 0.10 m against a 0.35 m capsule radius —
                //    below the radius, so the capsule rides over it instead of catching on it.
                (center_m: (-31.0, 0.0, 0.0), size_m: (32.0, 0.3, 26.0), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // the four walls. 10 m to the eaves, so the hall is 10 m in the clear — the
                // roof is the 1.5 m slab on top and the ridge lands on 11.5 m exactly, which is
                // `scale.ron: architecture.heights_m house_large`. **No invented height**: the
                // user has written 4.5 / 8 / 11.5 / 12 / 35 and nothing else, and a landmark
                // height for this building is a question for him (FIND-060 §2), not a number
                // for me. `landmark: false` therefore holds and the guard in tests/data.rs
                // still applies to it.
                //
                // ⚠️ All of them `anchorable: true`, and that is not laziness. The roof stands
                // over the centre of every one of them, and a tagged surface with something on
                // its roof centre is a lie in the map —
                // `tests/world.rs::f003_no_anchorable_block_has_another_block_sitting_on_its_roof_centre`.
                // **The roof is the anchor.**
                //
                // ⚠️ **This used to say "the interior is not tagged either … nothing outside can
                // reach an interior wall". Both halves are false since 2026-08-13.** All 31
                // interior blocks are anchorable now — the user: *"es ist extrem wichtig dass man
                // wirklich überall sein seil festmachen kann. also überall! ohne ausnahmen!"* —
                // and the reachability claim was simply wrong: `tests/world.rs::f019_the_tagged_interior_is_reachable_through_the_door`
                // measures a rope going straight in through the doorway from the street and
                // landing on `block_183` at x = −45.55, i.e. the back wall of the hall.
                // A tagged surface nothing can hook would still be a lie in the map (`FIND-059`);
                // that guard is what now proves this one is not.
                // west (back) wall — the canal side
                (center_m: (-46.25, 5.0, 0.0), size_m: (1.5, 10.0, 26.0), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // east facade, south of the door
                (center_m: (-15.75, 5.0, -8.0), size_m: (1.5, 10.0, 10.0), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // east facade, north of the door
                (center_m: (-15.75, 5.0, 8.0), size_m: (1.5, 10.0, 10.0), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // the lintel over the gate. It starts at y = 4.5, so the opening is **6 m wide
                // and 4.5 m high**: a 1.8 m player with a 0.35 m capsule walks through it
                // without aiming, and so does the cart the depot exists for.
                (center_m: (-15.75, 7.25, 0.0), size_m: (1.5, 5.5, 6.0), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // north and south walls, spanning only BETWEEN the two side walls: a corner
                // built twice is a z-fight and a doubled collider.
                (center_m: (-31.0, 5.0, 12.25), size_m: (29.0, 10.0, 1.5), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-31.0, 5.0, -12.25), size_m: (29.0, 10.0, 1.5), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // ⭐ the roof, and it is the one tagged surface of the building: 32 x 26 m of
                // sand_brown at 11.5 m, the colour every anchorable slab in this map wears.
                // Arriving by air is the natural way in — from the gantry beam at 60 m over the
                // street it is one shot, and the hall's own door is 15 m from the spawn point.
                (center_m: (-31.0, 10.75, 0.0), size_m: (32.0, 1.5, 26.0), color: "sand_brown", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // four posts carrying the roof of a 29 x 23 m hall. They stand at z = +-8, so
                // the aisle from the door to the back wall (z = -3..3) is 29 m of clear floor.
                (center_m: (-38.0, 5.0, -8.0), size_m: (2.0, 10.0, 2.0), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-24.0, 5.0, -8.0), size_m: (2.0, 10.0, 2.0), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-38.0, 5.0, 8.0), size_m: (2.0, 10.0, 2.0), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-24.0, 5.0, 8.0), size_m: (2.0, 10.0, 2.0), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // ---- The resupply, inside, against the back wall -----------------------
                // ⚠️ **Furniture, not stations.** These racks are what the player walks up
                // to; the `RefuelStation` entities that make them work are wired in
                // `src/mission/hub.rs` out of `missions.ron: hub.refuel_stations`, and that is a
                // separate hand. The coordinates they should take stand in `missions.ron` next
                // to the three that are still out on the pavement.
                //
                // ## ⭐ Two footprints, two SILHOUETTES — and why that is the whole fix
                //
                // Until 2026-08-13 both of them were literally the same line twice:
                // `size_m: (5, 1.2, 9), color: "brick_red"`. `FIND-080` lit the room and then
                // measured what the light could not buy: *"yes for 'those are boxes and they are
                // furniture', still no for 'that one is gas, that one is blades'"* — and the
                // pixels agreed, the two racks came out **identical to the level: 92.8 / 92.8,
                // 0.0 sRGB levels and 0.0 degrees of hue apart** (`f019-hq-racks-before.png`,
                // tick 592, mid-aisle looking west).
                //
                // ⚠️ **Colour is scarce here and shape is free.** The three signal colours
                // (cyan, amber, crimson) are gameplay only — a cyan gas rack is exactly the
                // "no cyan set dressing" rule this file keeps in two blocks so it can be a test
                // — and the palette holds five hues for the whole district. But every object in
                // this world is a cuboid, so a second cuboid costs nothing: **a row of fat
                // drums is not a row of thin plates**, at any distance, in any light, and for a
                // colour-blind player too.
                //
                // ⚠️ **The FOOTPRINTS are unchanged** — x = -44.5 .. -39.5, z = -11..-2 and
                // 2..11, and both bases still cover the whole 5 x 9 m at floor level. That is
                // deliberate: `missions.ron: hub.refuel_stations` puts the two triggers on the
                // AISLE FACES at (-42, 0.15, -+2), and `tests/mission.rs`
                // ::f019_a_supply_station_has_floor_you_can_actually_stand_on_inside_its_reach
                // scans standable 0.25 m cells against these solids. Nothing here moved in x or
                // z and nothing changed what a foot can stand on; only what an eye sees.
                //
                // ⚠️ **The face you build for is the +X face, not the +Z one.** The aisle runs
                // in X and both bays sit at its western end, so a player walking in sees the
                // 9 m long `+X` side of each — that is the two low bands in the "before" shot.
                // The first attempt gave the blades `size_m: (0.16, 1.5, 0.9)`, thin in X, and
                // they came out as six 0.9 m LOCKER DOORS: from the aisle you see the (y, z)
                // face, so **z is the width on screen and x is only the thickness**.
                //
                // ---- GAS, south of the aisle: four bottles on a skid ------------------
                // The Vector Gear's tanks. Fat, upright, repeated, wide-spaced — and each one
                // carries a narrower `stone_gray` collar on top, because a body plus a neck is
                // what makes a cuboid read as a pressure bottle instead of a crate.
                // `olive_green` is the only hue in the palette that is neither the stone of the
                // hall nor the wood of the bench opposite, and it is not a signal colour.
                //
                // The skid carries the floor footprint (0.15 .. 0.45 m); the bottles stand on
                // it and reach 2.60 m, so a 1.75 m eye looks UP at them.
                (center_m: (-42.0, 0.30, -6.5), size_m: (5.0, 0.3, 9.0), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // 2.4 m pitch, 1.3 m bottle: 1.1 m of air between each pair, and the row runs
                // the full 9 m of the bay. The nearest one stops at z = -2.25, clear of the
                // aisle and of the station trigger that sits on the face at z = -2.
                (center_m: (-42.0, 1.35, -10.1), size_m: (1.3, 1.8, 1.3), color: "olive_green", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-42.0, 1.35,  -7.7), size_m: (1.3, 1.8, 1.3), color: "olive_green", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-42.0, 1.35,  -5.3), size_m: (1.3, 1.8, 1.3), color: "olive_green", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-42.0, 1.35,  -2.9), size_m: (1.3, 1.8, 1.3), color: "olive_green", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // the collars — 0.5 m on a 1.3 m body, sitting ON it at 2.25 m and not in it.
                (center_m: (-42.0, 2.425, -10.1), size_m: (0.5, 0.35, 0.5), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-42.0, 2.425,  -7.7), size_m: (0.5, 0.35, 0.5), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-42.0, 2.425,  -5.3), size_m: (0.5, 0.35, 0.5), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-42.0, 2.425,  -2.9), size_m: (0.5, 0.35, 0.5), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                //
                // ---- BLADES, north of it: a bench, a back panel, five pairs -----------
                // The opposite reading in every axis: LOW where the gas is tall, MANY and THIN
                // where the gas is four fat bodies, PALE where the gas is dark. A blade is
                // 0.20 m of width and 1.3 m of height seen from the aisle — 1:6.5, which is a blade
                // and not a plank (0.35 x 0.9 was tried and read as a shelf board)
                // nobody mistakes it for a door, and they stand in **pairs**, 0.15 m apart,
                // because a Vector Gear carries two (`gear.ron: blades.start_pairs` is 5, and
                // that is exactly how many pairs hang here).
                (center_m: (-42.0, 0.55, 6.5), size_m: (5.0, 0.8, 9.0), color: "sand_brown", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // the panel stands ON the bench (0.95 .. 2.55 m), not through it — a coincident
                // face inside another box is a z-fight, and the two share the x = -44.5 plane.
                // Dark, because the blades in front of it are the pale thing.
                (center_m: (-44.2, 1.75, 6.5), size_m: (0.6, 1.6, 9.0), color: "brick_red", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                // ten blades = five pairs. 0.30 m inside a pair, 1.8 m from pair to pair, and
                // 0.125 m of air between the blades and the panel behind them.
                (center_m: (-43.75, 1.60,  2.75), size_m: (0.05, 1.3, 0.20), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-43.75, 1.60,  3.05), size_m: (0.05, 1.3, 0.20), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-43.75, 1.60,  4.55), size_m: (0.05, 1.3, 0.20), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-43.75, 1.60,  4.85), size_m: (0.05, 1.3, 0.20), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-43.75, 1.60,  6.35), size_m: (0.05, 1.3, 0.20), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-43.75, 1.60,  6.65), size_m: (0.05, 1.3, 0.20), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-43.75, 1.60,  8.15), size_m: (0.05, 1.3, 0.20), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-43.75, 1.60,  8.45), size_m: (0.05, 1.3, 0.20), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-43.75, 1.60,  9.95), size_m: (0.05, 1.3, 0.20), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),
                (center_m: (-43.75, 1.60, 10.25), size_m: (0.05, 1.3, 0.20), color: "stone_gray", anchorable: true, solid: true, landmark: false),

                // ---- Deleted 2026-08-12: the hand-placed row housing and the pocket ----
                // 75 detached boxes stood here — a 20 m pitch along the main street and a
                // 24 m pitch in the pocket, each one an island with an untagged ridge cap on
                // its roof centre. They were the 28 unhookable crowns of `FIND-059` and half
                // of "boxes on a lawn" in the screenshot of `FIND-056`.
                //
                // The closed-block layout builds both quarters now, at a 43 m block pitch
                // with party walls and a 7 m street, and it builds them denser than the hand
                // placement did. Whoever wants a pitched roof back builds it as body + cap
                // **with the cap anchorable and the body not** — a tagged surface with
                // something standing on its centre is a lie in the map, and
                // `tests/world.rs::f003_no_anchorable_block_has_another_block_sitting_on_its_roof_centre`
                // now says so out loud.
            ],

            // ================================================================================
            // THE LAMPS IN THE GARRISON HALL — the one interior in this map, and the reason
            // this list exists at all
            // ================================================================================
            //
            // The user, 2026-08-12: „auch das main gebäude in dem der gas und schwert nachschub
            // ist muss da sein (in das gebäude muss man rein laufen können. drinnen sind die
            // nachschübe)". You can walk in — `scripts/f019-hq.txt` proves it with 13 asserts —
            // and until today you could not SEE what was in there.
            //
            // `docs/FINDINGS.md` FIND-078 measured why, and the answer was not "it is dark":
            // the hall's back wall read 51.9 and an EXTERIOR wall in shadow read 51.5 in the
            // same frame. A roofed room is not darker than a shadow; it has nothing bright to
            // read against. Ambient cannot fix that — 5x the fill buys 5.8 sRGB levels, costs
            // the exterior its shadows 1:1, and at 12000 the racks are still flat rectangles,
            // because a directionless fill gives nothing a lit face and a dark one.
            //
            // ## The geometry these two numbers are derived from
            //
            //   hall interior   x = -45.5 .. -16.5   z = -11.5 .. 11.5   floor 0.15, ceiling 10
            //   gate            x = -16.5 .. -15     z = -3 .. 3         4.5 m to the lintel
            //   the racks       x = -44.5 .. -39.5   z = -11..-2 and 2..11, 1.35 m tall
            //   the aisle       z = -3 .. 3, clear from the door to the back wall
            //
            // Both lamps hang at **y = 8.5** — 1.5 m under the roof slab, over the aisle at
            // z = 0, so each rack is lit from ABOVE AND FROM THE SIDE. That is the whole point:
            // the top face and the aisle flank come up, the outboard flank stays on the fill,
            // and a box with two values is a shape instead of a rectangle.
            //
            // ## ⚠️ Why this does not brighten one pixel of the district
            //
            // A point light without shadows is unoccluded — it reaches every fragment inside
            // `range_m`, wall or no wall. It is **Lambert** that contains it, not the wall: the
            // OUTER face of every wall of this hall points away from a lamp inside it, so
            // `NdotL <= 0` and it takes nothing at any range. The faces that could leak are the
            // ones pointing UP — street, aprons, quays — and `range_m` is what keeps those out,
            // because Bevy's attenuation `(1 - (d/r)^4)^2 / d^2` is a HARD cut-off at d = r.
            //
            // Measured against every one of the 232 placed blocks of this map: the nearest
            // exterior surface that faces either lamp at all is the ground slab's top at y = 0
            // directly beneath it — and that is buried under the hall's own 0.3 m floor. The
            // nearest exterior surface anyone can SEE is the street apron at x = -15:
            //   lamp east  d = 14.68 m  vs range 11.0   (3.7 m of margin)
            //   lamp west  d = 23.6 m   vs range 14.0   (9.6 m of margin)
            //
            // ## ⚠️ `shadows: false`, and that is the measured choice
            //
            // A shadow-casting point light costs a CUBE map: six depth passes over everything
            // in range, per light, per frame (`docs/lessons/performance.md` rule 5 — the switch
            // that is never thrown without a number). The hall holds four posts and two racks
            // and no occluder whose shadow carries information; the racks shade their own far
            // side by Lambert alone, which is the cue that was missing. Two shadowless lamps
            // measured 0.0 ms against the same scene without them.
            lights: [
                // WEST — over the aisle between the two racks. This is the lamp that makes the
                // back of the hall the bright thing the racks read against, and that puts a lit
                // top edge on each of them.
                (center_m: (-37.0, 8.5, 0.0), color: "lamp_warm", intensity_lm: 35000000.0, range_m: 14.0, shadows: false),
                // EAST — over the walk in from the gate, so the floor ahead of a player who
                // steps through the door is lit and the room has depth instead of one far wall.
                // Its range is the tighter of the two only because it stands 12 m from the
                // door: 11.0 keeps the sphere off the street apron with 3.7 m to spare.
                (center_m: (-27.0, 8.5, 0.0), color: "lamp_warm", intensity_lm: 35000000.0, range_m: 11.0, shadows: false),
            ],
        ),
    },
)
